+Geometry Consistency Loss is a regularization technique introduced in the INS framework to enforce view-consistent scene geometry during 3D style transfer [S1]. It divides the radiance field representation into a style implicit module and a content implicit module, which are fused through an amalgamation module [S1]. The method applies a self-distilled loss to regularize the stylized scene's geometry against the original content [S1]. It builds on the differentiable rendering principles of [Geometric and Normal Alignment Losses](4970-geometric-and-normal-alignment-losses.md).
 
